  </div></div> <!----> <!----></div></div> </div><span class="el-popover__reference-wrapper"><span class="iconfont icon-Search_icon text-[20px] cursor-pointer text-[#444444]" data-v-22dae327></span></span></span></div> <div class="el-badge cursor-pointer custom-nav-el-badge sm:hidden no-num-show" data-v-118d177b><a href="https://cart.jlcpcb.com/shopcart/cart" class="no-underline" data-v-118d177b><i class="iconfont icon-shopping text-24 text-222222" data-v-118d177b></i></a><sup class="el-badge__content is-fixed">0</sup></div> <a href="https://cart.jlcpcb.com/quote?spm=jlcpcb.Public.2006" class="no-underline hover:text-primary border-1 border-solid rounded-[24px] inline-flex items-center px-12 h-[34px] sm:hidden text-primary border-primary" data-v-118d177b><span data-v-118d177b>Order Now</span></a> <span data-v-118d177b><div role="tooltip" id="el-popover-4550" aria-hidden="true" class="el-popover el-popper mt-10 px-20 pt-6 pb-10 top-[50px] nav-global-style-user__popover" style="width:undefinedpx;display:none;"><!----><div data-v-118d177b><!----></div> </div><span class="el-popover__reference-wrapper"><div id="home_sign in" data-v-118d177b><span class="cursor-pointer sign-in-btn sm:hidden" data-v-118d177b>
            Sign In
            <!----></span> <span class="hidden sm:inline-block" data-v-118d177b><span class="sign-in-btn" data-v-118d177b>
              Sign In
            </span></span></div></span></span></div></div> <div tabindex="-1" class="el-drawer__wrapper" style="display:none;" data-v-3bb9afe7 data-v-118d177b><div role="document" tabindex="-1" class="el-drawer__container"><div aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="el-drawer__title" aria-label="" role="dialog" tabindex="-1" class="el-drawer ltr small-screen-nav-menu__drawer" style="width:30%;"><header id="el-drawer__title" class="el-drawer__header"><span role="heading" title=""></span><!----></header><!----></div></div></div> <!----></nav> <main main-content class="flex-1 flex-basis-auto relative" data-v-f507df84><div style="position:relative;background:#fff url() no-repeat center/100% 100%;height:3300px;" data-v-e3b55878 data-v-f507df84><div class="low-code-render-container" data-v-e3b55878><div id="" style="position:absolute;width:100%;height:13.333333333333334%;left:0%;top:0%;transform:rotateZ(0deg);z-index:2;" data-v-e3b55878><div id="" class="BannerComponent public-style banner-padding" style="background:rgba(5, 254, 229, 1) url() no-repeat center/100% 100%;text-align:left;" data-v-25539b9f data-v-e3b55878><div class="text-area" data-v-25539b9f><div class="text-area-content" data-v-25539b9f><h2 class="title" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,1);" data-v-25539b9f>PCB Thickness</h2><p class="desc-text" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,1);" data-v-25539b9f>The thickness of PCBs impacts the performance, stability, and reliability of the final electronic products. Now, JLCPCB offers a variety of PCB thickness options to help you make the best and affordable choice. Thickness from 0.8mm to 1.6mm starts at only $2.</p><div id="" class="coupon-box public-style" data-v-2457f1d2 data-v-25539b9f><!----><p class="coupon-left-money" style="color:#8d7503;" data-v-2457f1d2><span class="text-18" data-v-2457f1d2>$</span><span class="text-44" data-v-2457f1d2>6</span></p><div class="coupon-right-title" data-v-2457f1d2><h2 class="text-24 font-semibold" style="color:#8d7503;" data-v-2457f1d2>PCB Coupon</h2><p class="coupon-right-date" style="color:rgba(208, 189, 41,1);" data-v-2457f1d2>Valid for 30 days</p><div class="get-coupon-btn cursor-pointer" data-v-2457f1d2><span class="btn-text" style="color:rgba(255, 255, 255,1);" data-v-2457f1d2>Get It Now</span><span class="btn-icon" data-v-2457f1d2><i class="el-icon-arrow-right" data-v-2457f1d2></i></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div id="" style="position:absolute;width:100%;height:18.181818181818183%;left:0%;top:16.666666666666664%;transform:rotateZ(0deg);z-index:3;" data-v-e3b55878><div id="" class="imgTextComponent public-style" style="background-color:rgba(255, 255, 255, 1);" data-v-22d68ebc data-v-e3b55878><div class="show-area" data-v-22d68ebc><div class="img-area cursor-pointer" data-v-22d68ebc><img src="https://static.jlcpcb.com/assets/decorate/6bde7a14200e443297ed804822b2bd60.jpg" width="100%" alt="" data-v-22d68ebc></div><div class="text-area" style="color:#222222;" data-v-22d68ebc><h2 class="text-area-title" style="color:#222222;" data-v-22d68ebc>Characteristics of PCB Thickness</h2><!----><ul class="text-area-content" data-v-22d68ebc><li class="text-area-content-item" data-v-22d68ebc><p class="mr-8" data-v-22d68ebc><i class="el-icon-success text-2B8CED" data-v-22d68ebc></i></p><p data-v-22d68ebc><span class="font-semibold" data-v-22d68ebc>Ultra-thin PCB (below 0.6 mm):</span><span data-v-22d68ebc> Ultra-thin PCBs are lightweight, soft, and easy to bend, making them suitable for products that require a high level of space efficiency, such as smartphones, wearable devices and drones. </span></p></li><li class="text-area-content-item" data-v-22d68ebc><p class="mr-8" data-v-22d68ebc><i class="el-icon-success text-2B8CED" data-v-22d68ebc></i></p><p data-v-22d68ebc><span class="font-semibold" data-v-22d68ebc>Mid-Range Thin PCBs (0.6-1.6 mm):</span><span data-v-22d68ebc> The mid-range PCB has a good balance between thickness and load-bearing capacity, making it suitable for a wide range of electronic products, including computer motherboards and home appliance control boards. </span></p></li><li class="text-area-content-item" data-v-22d68ebc><p class="mr-8" data-v-22d68ebc><i class="el-icon-success text-2B8CED" data-v-22d68ebc></i></p><p data-v-22d68ebc><span class="font-semibold" data-v-22d68ebc>Thicker PCBs (above 1.6 mm):</span><span data-v-22d68ebc> Thick boards have a high load-bearing capacity and stiffness, making them suitable for harsh environments and electronic products that require the carrying of high-power and heavy components. </span></p></li></ul><!----></div></div></div></div><div id="" style="position:absolute;width:100%;height:16.666666666666664%;left:0%;top:35.15151515151515%;transform:rotateZ(0deg);z-index:4;" data-v-e3b55878><div id="" class="imgTextComponent public-style" style="background-color:#fff;" data-v-22d68ebc data-v-e3b55878><div class="show-area row-reverse" data-v-22d68ebc><div class="img-area cursor-pointer" data-v-22d68ebc><img src="https://static.jlcpcb.com/assets/decorate/e651ee6fd1c54c229724275beda3aaf9.png" width="100%" alt="" data-v-22d68ebc></div><div class="text-area" style="color:#222222;" data-v-22d68ebc><h2 class="text-area-title" style="color:#222222;" data-v-22d68ebc>Key factors affecting PCB Thickness</h2><p class="text-area-content" data-v-22d68ebc> Circuit board thickness is influenced by PCB layer count, signal type, material selection, operating environment, copper thickness, and special requirements. More copper layers increase thickness. High-power signals demand thicker copper layers and wider traces; low-power environments can use thinner boards. Material choice and operating conditions impact thickness. Copper thickness, such as 2 or 3 ounces, significantly affects overall thickness. Special applications, like high-density boards, may require customized thickness for unique environments. </p><!----><!----></div></div></div></div><div id="" style="position:absolute;width:100%;height:18.181818181818183%;left:0%;top:51.81818181818182%;transform:rotateZ(0deg);z-index:5;" data-v-e3b55878><div id="" class="imgTextComponent public-style" style="background-color:#fff;" data-v-22d68ebc data-v-e3b55878><div class="show-area" data-v-22d68ebc><div class="img-area cursor-pointer" data-v-22d68ebc><img src="https://static.jlcpcb.com/assets/decorate/bcf8da5ad0b14839ad6a2d11b68fe6ef.png" width="100%" alt="" data-v-22d68ebc></div><div class="text-area" style="color:#222222;" data-v-22d68ebc><h2 class="text-area-title" style="color:#222222;" data-v-22d68ebc>How to Choose the Appropriate PCB Thickness</h2><!----><ul class="text-area-content" data-v-22d68ebc><li class="text-area-content-item" data-v-22d68ebc><p class="mr-8" data-v-22d68ebc><i class="el-icon-success text-2B8CED" data-v-22d68ebc></i></p><p data-v-22d68ebc><span class="font-semibold" data-v-22d68ebc>Application Focus:</span><span data-v-22d68ebc> Before deciding on PCB thickness, understanding application needs, scenarios, and component loads is crucial.This ensures the chosen thickness aligns with product requirements. </span></p></li><li class="text-area-content-item" data-v-22d68ebc><p class="mr-8" data-v-22d68ebc><i class="el-icon-success text-2B8CED" data-v-22d68ebc></i></p><p data-v-22d68ebc><span class="font-semibold" data-v-22d68ebc>Safety Concerns:</span><span data-v-22d68ebc> If the circuit board needs to withstand high voltage or current, it is important to select a thicker circuit board to ensure its safe operation. </span></p></li><li class="text-area-content-item" data-v-22d68ebc><p class="mr-8" data-v-22d68ebc><i class="el-icon-success text-2B8CED" data-v-22d68ebc></i></p><p data-v-22d68ebc><span class="font-semibold" data-v-22d68ebc>Mechanical Strength:</span><span data-v-22d68ebc> If the circuit board needs to withstand high mechanical influence, it is advisable to choose a thicker PCB to ensure its mechanical strength </span></p></li></ul><!----></div></div></div></div><div id="" style="position:absolute;width:100%;height:10.606060606060606%;left:0%;top:70%;transform:rotateZ(0deg);z-index:6;" data-v-e3b55878><div id="" class="benefitsComponent public-style" style="background-color:#fff;" data-v-4b7e6eec data-v-e3b55878><div class="container" data-v-4b7e6eec><h2 class="container-title font-semibold" style="color:rgba(22, 22, 22,1);" data-v-4b7e6eec> Why Choose JLCPCB </h2><ul class="benefits-list" data-v-4b7e6eec><li class="benefits-list-item" data-v-4b7e6eec><p class="benefits-list-item-title" data-v-4b7e6eec><img src="https://static.jlcpcb.com/assets/decorate/224738ed240e40a1b1983251c17067c5.png" alt="icon" class="benefits-list-item-icon align-middle" data-v-4b7e6eec><span class="font-semibold align-middle" style="color:rgba(22, 22, 22,1);" data-v-4b7e6eec> Easy Ordering Process </span></p><p style="color:rgba(22, 22, 22,1);" data-v-4b7e6eec> Upload your Gerber file and then get an instant quote! Easy as online shopping. </p></li><li class="benefits-list-item" data-v-4b7e6eec><p class="benefits-list-item-title" data-v-4b7e6eec><img src="https://static.jlcpcb.com/assets/decorate/4f877738980a4d3a9842683124cd1655.png" alt="icon" class="benefits-list-item-icon align-middle" data-v-4b7e6eec><span class="font-semibold align-middle" style="color:rgba(22, 22, 22,1);" data-v-4b7e6eec> Affordable Manufacturing </span></p><p style="color:rgba(22, 22, 22,1);" data-v-4b7e6eec> Get 1-8 layer PCBs for just $2! Efficient large-scale production offers unbeatable prices. </p></li><li class="benefits-list-item" data-v-4b7e6eec><p class="benefits-list-item-title" data-v-4b7e6eec><img src="https://static.jlcpcb.com/assets/decorate/98fc29f7eb4f4de283243840f1b56f88.png" alt="icon" class="benefits-list-item-icon align-middle" data-v-4b7e6eec><span class="font-semibold align-middle" style="color:rgba(22, 22, 22,1);" data-v-4b7e6eec> Reliable Services </span></p><p style="color:rgba(22, 22, 22,1);" data-v-4b7e6eec> In-house production with strict quality control. Fast PCB production in just 24 hours! </p></li></ul></div></div></div><div style="position:absolute;width:100%;height:4.848484848484849%;left:0%;top:95.15151515151516%;transform:rotateZ(0deg);z-index:7;" data-v-e3b55878><div id="" class="streamerComponent public-style" style="background:#fff url(https://static.jlcpcb.com/assets/decorate/c3f17a8fafdd4b91b5f36c09066ecce7.png) no-repeat center/cover;" data-v-3bb48ad5 data-v-e3b55878><section class="container" data-v-3bb48ad5><h2 class="streamer-title font-semibold text-2B8CED" style="color:#2b8ced !important;" data-v-3bb48ad5>Choose Your PCB Thickness Now</h2><div id="" class="button-box public-style" style="background-color:#2b8ced;border-radius:30px;" data-v-019dba28 data-v-3bb48ad5><span class="button-text" style="color:#ffffff;" data-v-019dba28>Get Instant Quote</span><span class="button-icon" data-v-019dba28><i class="el-icon-arrow-right" style="color:#2b8ced;" data-v-019dba28></i></span></div></section></div></div><div id="" style="position:absolute;width:100%;height:13.636363636363635%;left:0%;top:80.60606060606061%;transform:rotateZ(0deg);z-index:8;" data-v-e3b55878><div id="" isUpdateNum="19" class="FaqComponent public-style" data-v-15dab343 data-v-e3b55878><div class="faq-container" data-v-15dab343><h2 class="title" style="color:#222222;" data-v-15dab343> Frequently Asked Questions
 </h2><ul class="faq-list" data-v-15dab343><li data-v-15dab343><div class="faq-list-item" data-v-15dab343><span style="color:#222222;" data-v-15dab343>What PCB thicknesses does JLCPCB offer?</span><span class="panel-icon-plus" data-v-15dab343><i class="el-icon-plus" data-v-15dab343></i></span></div><div class="questions-content overflow-hidden h-1" data-v-15dab343><p class="foldablePanel" data-v-15dab343>We offer the following thickness options: 0.4mm, 0.6mm, 0.8mm, 1.0mm, 1.2mm, 1.6mm, 2.0mm. Note that 2-layer PCBs with 0.6mm thickness do not support HASL (with lead) surface finish.</p></div><div class="border-b" data-v-15dab343></div></li><li data-v-15dab343><div class="faq-list-item" data-v-15dab343><span style="color:undefined;" data-v-15dab343>What is the thickness tolerance of your PCBs?</span><span class="panel-icon-plus" data-v-15dab343><i class="el-icon-plus" data-v-15dab343></i></span></div><div class="questions-content overflow-hidden h-1" data-v-15dab343><p class="foldablePanel" data-v-15dab343>The thickness tolerance of our PCBs is +/-10% of the finished board thickness.</p></div><div class="border-b" data-v-15dab343></div></li><li data-v-15dab343><div class="faq-list-item" data-v-15dab343><span style="color:undefined;" data-v-15dab343>Anything I should know when selecting 0.4mm thickness boards?</span><span class="panel-icon-plus" data-v-15dab343><i class="el-icon-plus" data-v-15dab343></i></span></div><div class="questions-content overflow-hidden h-1" data-v-15dab343><p class="foldablePanel" data-v-15dab343>For 0.4mm thickness boards, only ENIG finish is accepted. These boards cannot be made with a panel and are not available for 1-layer PCBs.</p></div><div class="border-b" data-v-15dab343></div></li><li data-v-15dab343><div class="faq-list-item" data-v-15dab343><span style="color:undefined;" data-v-15dab343>Anything I should know when selecting 0.6mm thickness boards?</span><span class="panel-icon-plus" data-v-15dab343><i class="el-icon-plus" data-v-15dab343></i></span></div><div class="questions-content overflow-hidden h-1" data-v-15dab343><p class="foldablePanel" data-v-15dab343>Boards with 0.6mm thickness have a maximum size of 100mm x 100mm. This thickness is not available for 1-layer, 4-layer, or 6-layer PCBs.</p></div><div class="border-b" data-v-15dab343></div></li><li data-v-15dab343><div class="faq-list-item" data-v-15dab343><span style="color:undefined;" data-v-15dab343>Anything I should know when selecting 0.8-1.0mm thickness boards?</span><span class="panel-icon-plus" data-v-15dab343><i class="el-icon-plus" data-v-15dab343></i></span></div><div class="questions-content overflow-hidden h-1" data-v-15dab343><p class="foldablePanel" data-v-15dab343>For boards with 0.8mm to 1.0mm thickness, the maximum size is 300mm x 300mm.</p></div><div class="border-b" data-v-15dab343></div></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></main> <footer id="frontFooter" class="bg-[#26272A] pt-50 pb-30 md:pt-20 sm:pt-20 text-14 text-white" data-v-4659cd07 data-v-f507df84><div class="jlc-content" data-v-4659cd07><div class="flex justify-between md:hidden sm:hidden" data-v-4659cd07><div class="flex flex-col justify-between" data-v-4659cd07><div class="text-16 font-medium cursor-pointer flex items-center hover:text-primary" data-v-4659cd07><i class="iconfont text-20 mr-4 icon-chat" data-v-4659cd07></i>
          Online Chat &gt;
